  {
   "id": "cap-bcl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1450,
   "width": 2600,
   "height": 64,
   "text": "routed experts 256×75 **22.65B** (56.2%) · MLA attention ×78 **12.87B** (31.9%) · shared expert + router ×75 **2.95B** (7.3%) · dense FFN ×3 **679.5M** (1.7%) · lm head **951.6M** (2.4%) · DSA indexers ×21 **196.8M** (0.5%) · embed **0** (row lookup) · MTP block **0** (speculative drafting only)"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "# GLM-5.3 — model  \nOne continuous decoder-only stack L0–77, read top → bottom; layers that repeat are drawn once with **×N**. **Grey bars = tensors**, length ∝ channels per token (0.08 px/channel). **Boxes = operations**, all one size; where parameters and compute live is the pair of bars above. T = sequence length. *Layer* tab = one decoder layer in detail."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 450,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "Every layer = **MLA attention** (64 heads, KV squeezed to a 512+64 latent) made sparse by **DSA**: each query attends only the top 2048 past tokens chosen by a small indexer.    \nRow colours — **amber**: dense SwiGLU FFN + own indexer (L0–2) · **cyan**: MoE + own indexer · **grey**: MoE, *reuses* the top-2048 picks of the cyan layer above (no indexer weights). MoE = 8 of 256 routed experts + 1 shared, sigmoid router. The barcode on the right lists every layer in order."
  },
  {
   "id": "raw1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**raw text**  \"The cat sat…\"",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
